1. Introduction
E-commerce websites contain a large amount of product information that can be useful for market analysis and business decision-making. Web scraping is an automated technique used to extract such information from websites.

In this project, data was collected from the "Books to Scrape" website using Python. After collecting the data, it was cleaned, analyzed, and visualized using Python libraries and Power BI. The project demonstrates how web scraping can help businesses understand product pricing, availability, and market trends.

2. Objectives
Collect product information from an e-commerce website.
Clean and organize the extracted dataset.
Perform exploratory data analysis.
Create visualizations for better understanding.
Build an interactive Power BI dashboard.
Generate business insights from the collected data.

3. Problem Statement
Businesses need accurate product information to analyze pricing strategies and customer trends. Manually collecting this information is time-consuming and inefficient.

This project automates the data collection process using web scraping techniques and provides useful insights through data visualization.

